;===========================================================
; 01d_params_lab.fis
;
; LABORATORY VALIDATION parameter set - own test programme.
;
; SEPARATE from 01_parameters.fis (Gai & Sanchez verification)
; and 01c_params_kennedy.fis (Kennedy 2023 external
; validation). Neither of those is modified. Never call more
; than ONE of the three parameter files in the same FLAC
; session - the second would silently overwrite the first.
;
; VARIABLE NAMING - IMPORTANT
; The names below are the ones 02_m_eicp.fis actually reads.
; They are not free to rename. Requested labels that differ:
;   $kappa_p  requested as $kappa_p   (same)
;   $m_cs     requested as $M_cs
;   $ds_p     requested as $Ds_p
;   $ini_e    requested as $ini_e
; FISH is case-insensitive so $M_cs and $Ds_p would in fact
; resolve, but the canonical spellings are used here for
; consistency with the other two parameter files.
;===========================================================
;
def eicp_par_lab
;
;-----------------------------------------------------------
; HOST SAND PARAMETERS
;
; DECLARED ASSUMPTIONS, NOT MEASUREMENTS.
; kappa and lambda are assumptions, not results of this test
; programme:
;   kappa - the unload/reload (US-KL) stage was DROPPED, so no
;           swelling line was measured. Value carried over from
;           Gai & Sanchez (2019) Table 1.
;   lambda - not measurable at the stress levels used here. A
;           normal compression line cannot be identified from
;           triaxial shearing alone; it needs isotropic
;           compression to stresses well beyond pc. Value
;           carried over from Gai & Sanchez Table 1.
; Both must be reported as assumptions in the write-up. They
; are the principal caveat on this validation, exactly as for
; the Kennedy series.
;-----------------------------------------------------------
    $kappa_p  = 0.003        ; ASSUMED (US-KL stage dropped)
    $lambda_p = 0.25         ; ASSUMED (not measurable here)
    $ds_p     = 0.04         ; published (Gai Table 1)
    $nu_p     = 0.17         ; published (Gai Table 1)
;
;   eta - ASSUMED, AND FOUND NOT TO TRANSFER TO THIS SAND.
;   eta sets the rate at which the sub-loading ratio R grows
;   (Eq. 6, dR = -eta ln(R) |dep|), and therefore the STRAIN
;   SCALE of the response: how much straining is needed for
;   the sub-loading surface to inflate out to the stress path.
;
;   Phase A found the model's peak at 4.5 % axial strain
;   against a measured 2.45 % - 1.84x too late - with the
;   magnitude correct to -2.6 %. The phase transformation is
;   likewise 1.63x late (4.0 % against 2.45 %). R is growing
;   too slowly, so eta = 60 is too LOW for this sand; a higher
;   eta would move the peak earlier without altering its
;   magnitude, since eta does not enter the surface size.
;
;   RETAINED UNCHANGED at the published value. The strain-scale
;   mismatch is reported as an eta-transferability finding, not
;   corrected - correcting it would convert a prediction into a
;   two-parameter fit.
;
;   This is the SECOND assumed-and-published parameter found
;   not to transfer, alongside a = 200 kPa (Kennedy series:
;   over-predicts the EICP cementation increment by ~2.1x).
;   Both were calibrated on MICP-treated Ottawa sand. Together
;   they bound what can be carried over from Gai & Sanchez:
;   the FORM of the model transfers, the CALIBRATION does not.
    $eta_p    = 60.0         ; published; see note above
;
;-----------------------------------------------------------
; CRITICAL STATE SLOPE - M = 1.09 RETAINED
;
; M is NOT calibrated from this test programme, and it cannot
; be: both specimens were STILL SOFTENING at the 20 % axial
; strain termination, with
;     dq/d(epsilon_a) = -3.47 kPa/%  and  -1.29 kPa/%
;
; A specimen still softening has not reached critical state,
; so its stress ratio eta = q/p' is still FALLING toward M.
; The end-of-test eta is therefore an UPPER BOUND on M, not an
; estimate of it. The binding (smallest) upper bound from the
; two specimens is
;     M <= 1.147
;
; The published Gai & Sanchez value M = 1.09 satisfies that
; constraint, so it is retained unchanged. This is a genuine
; consistency check, not a fit: the data constrain M from one
; side only and 1.09 lies inside the admissible range.
;
; REPORT IT AS SUCH. Do not describe 1.147 as a measured M -
; it is a bound. Had 1.09 exceeded it, the published value
; would have been falsified; it does not.
;
; Contrast with the Kennedy series, where phi'_res = 34.43 deg
; was obtained from a specimen at residual with c' = 0, giving
; a genuine measurement of M = 1.393 and a real mismatch.
;-----------------------------------------------------------
    $m_cs     = 1.09         ; retained; measured bound M <= 1.147
;
;-----------------------------------------------------------
; CEMENTATION PARAMETERS - APPLIED BLIND
;
; Published Gai & Sanchez (2019) Table 2 values, calibrated on
; MICP-treated Ottawa sand, applied here WITHOUT adjustment.
; a is the quantity under test in the treated phase: the
; Kennedy series found it over-predicts EICP cementation by a
; factor of about 2.1 at a clean comparison point.
;-----------------------------------------------------------
;
;   a - PHASE D BRACKETING STUDY IN PROGRESS.
;   Phase C applied the published a = 200 kPa blind and
;   over-predicted the cementation gain by 8.2x (+68.1 %
;   model against +8.3 % measured). Phase D brackets the
;   effective value by trial:
;     C   a = 200000 Pa  pb = 534.0 kPa  gain +68.1 %  ev -8.00 %
;     D1  a =  50000 Pa  pb = 133.5 kPa  gain +18.1 %  ev -4.50 %
;     D2  a =  25000 Pa  pb =  66.8 kPa  R0 = 0.1898  (current)
;     D3  a =  12500 Pa  pb =  33.4 kPa  R0 = 0.2027
;     --  a =      0 Pa  pb =   0.0 kPa  gain  0      ev -3.10 %
;   All trials remain on the DRY side at sigma3 = 100 kPa
;   (dry while q < 590 / 490 / 440 kPa against a 258 kPa
;   target), so each run yields a usable peak.
;
;   GAIN IS LINEAR IN a over 50-200 kPa: scaling D1 up by 4
;   predicts +72.4 % against +68.1 % observed, i.e. 6 %
;   sublinear. Interpolating D1 to the +8.3 % target gives
;   a ~ 23 kPa, so the answer is bracketed between D3 and D2.
;
;   DILATION FLOOR - THE DECISIVE RESULT.
;   Volumetric strain at 20 % is MONOTONE in a:
;     a =      0 : -3.10 %   <- the floor
;     a =  50000 : -4.50 %
;     a = 200000 : -8.00 %
;   More cementation always means MORE dilation, because pb
;   enters only through p0 = R(pc + pb) and a larger surface
;   drives the stress point further onto the dry side. The
;   least-dilative state the model can reach for a treated
;   specimen is therefore the a = 0 untreated value, -3.10 %.
;   Measured ET-100 is -2.35 %, which lies BELOW that floor.
;
;   NO NON-NEGATIVE a CAN REACH IT. a < 0 is outside the
;   formulation's admissible domain - it would mean cementation
;   shrinking the yield surface, and p0 could go negative and
;   invert the surface. So this is not a hidden option.
;
;   The hypothesis was stated BEFORE D1 was run and is now
;   confirmed numerically across three values of a: the
;   strength gain can be matched, the dilation cannot, at any
;   admissible a.
;
;   THIS IS A DOCUMENTED SENSITIVITY, NOT A RECALIBRATION.
;   a = 200 kPa remains the validation case. RESTORE IT when
;   Phase D is finished - the Phase A-C results depend on it.
;
;   Back-calculating a from the gain is INVALID. The pc/pb
;   coupling has now been demonstrated in three independent
;   contexts (Gai mu study, Gai a study, and the pc evolution
;   across the lab confinements). Bracket by trial.
    $a_pa     = 25000.0      ; PHASE D2 (published 200000.0)
    $mu_p     = 6.5          ; published
;
;-----------------------------------------------------------
; INITIAL STATE
;
; e0 is set per specimen by set_case in the driver, from the
; measured value. $ini_e below is only the UDM's internal
; fallback for a zone with no m_e assigned.
;-----------------------------------------------------------
    $ini_e    = 0.740        ; fallback; US-100 measured value
    $ini_r    = 0.01         ; fallback; ini_eicp_r recomputes R0
;                              from the actual stress state
    $ini_chi  = 1.0          ; intact bonding at t = 0
;
;-----------------------------------------------------------
; PRE-CONSOLIDATION PRESSURE - THE SOLE FITTED PARAMETER
;
; pc is the ONLY quantity fitted in this validation. It is
; calibrated against the UNTREATED specimen US-100 alone.
; Everything else is either published (M, Ds, nu, eta, a, mu)
; or a declared assumption (kappa, lambda).
;
; Consequence: every treated run is a PREDICTION, not a fit.
; Do NOT re-tune pc per specimen, per confinement or per
; calcite content. Later confinements, if any, are
; cross-validation of this single value.
;
; CALIBRATED: 460,000 Pa - ACCEPTED at Phase A trial 1.
;
; CALIBRATION BASIS
;   Specimen:  US-100, UNTREATED (mc = 0), e0 = 0.740 measured
;   Confining: sigma3 = 100 kPa
;   R0 = sigma3/pc = 100000/460000 = 0.2174 (pb = 0)
;
;   PEAK MAGNITUDE - PASS
;     Target 238.1 kPa, acceptance band 228-248 kPa
;     Model  232 kPa          -> -2.6 %, within band
;
;   STRAIN TO PEAK - FAIL, recorded as a finding
;     Target 2.45 %,  Model 4.5 %   -> 1.84x too late
;
;   VOLUMETRIC RESPONSE
;     Measured -3.67 % at 20 %,  Model -3.10 %
;     Phase transformation: measured 2.45 %, model 4.0 %
;                                        -> 1.63x too late
;
;   The two strain stretches (1.84x on peak, 1.63x on phase
;   transformation) agree to within 13 % of each other and
;   share the same sign, which is strong support for ONE
;   underlying effect on the strain scale rather than two
;   independent errors. Quote both; the mean is ~1.7x.
;
;   t_ev VERIFIED INDEPENDENTLY against deformed geometry:
;     r = 1.135, h = 0.800 -> V = 3.2376 against V0 = 3.1416
;     geometric ev = -3.06 % against t_ev -3.10 %  AGREE
;   The void-ratio route is therefore sound. (t_vsi was
;   misdefined - FLAC's vsi is a per-step increment, not an
;   accumulated total - and is discarded. The geometric check
;   above replaces it.)
;
;   Servo held 100,050-100,075 Pa against a 100,000 Pa target
;   (0.05-0.08 %). Unbalanced force zero throughout.
;
; NOTE on calibrating pc: there is no valid closed-form route
; from a target peak strength to pc. R, pc, chi and the
; dilation response evolve in a coupled way during shearing -
; demonstrated in both parameter directions during the Gai mu
; and a sensitivity studies, and the reason a closed-form
; derivation was rejected for the Kennedy series after it
; overshot by a factor of 3.9. Calibrate by trial, judging
; BOTH peak magnitude AND strain-to-peak.
;
; DO NOT RE-TUNE. Every later run - other confinements, any
; treated specimen - is cross-validation or prediction against
; this single value.
;
; ---- PHASE B CROSS-VALIDATION AT sigma3 = 200 kPa: FAILS
;      QUALITATIVELY ----
;
; Same pc, same sand, same density, mc = 0. Result: the model
; produced NO PEAK. q rose to 270 kPa at 6 % and kept climbing
; to 315 kPa at 20 %. Measured US-200 peaks at 531.8 kPa at
; 5.03 % with a 6.7 % post-peak drop.
;   Magnitude: 315 against 531.8 kPa, -41 %
;   Scaling:   model 1.36 against measured 2.23 (100 -> 200)
;
; CAUSE - the specimen is on the WRONG SIDE OF CRITICAL STATE.
; Critical state sits at p' = p0/2. With mc = 0 (pb = 0) and
; R -> 1, p0 = pc = 460 kPa, so the boundary is p' = 230 kPa.
; On the drained path p' = sigma3 + q/3 the dry-side condition
; p' < 230 kPa becomes q < 3(230 - sigma3):
;     sigma3 = 100 kPa : dry while q <  390 kPa
;                        (peak occurs at 232 kPa -> DRY, correct)
;     sigma3 = 200 kPa : dry while q <   90 kPa
;                        (q passes 90 kPa almost immediately
;                         -> WET for the whole test, wrong)
; A wet-side specimen compacts and hardens monotonically. It
; cannot peak, so no peak is possible at this confinement with
; this pc. Both real specimens were dense and dilatant.
;
; CONFIRMED BY THE MODEL'S OWN INTERNALS - two independent
; readouts, neither used in the diagnosis:
;   pc evolution (sign of dpc is the cleanest side indicator):
;     sigma3 = 100 : 460 -> 470 -> 368 kPa  (erodes  = dry)
;     sigma3 = 200 : 460 -> 520 -> 576 kPa  (rises   = wet)
;   stress ratio eta:
;     sigma3 = 100 : overshoots then descends, 1.32 -> 1.20
;     sigma3 = 200 : approaches M = 1.09 from BELOW, 1.02 at
;                    20 % and still rising
;
; THIS IS A QUALITATIVE FAILURE, AND STRONGER THAN ANYTHING IN
; THE KENNEDY SERIES. There the same fixed-pc limitation gave
; magnitude errors only (-1 %, +47 %, +146 %) because
; pc = 1350 kPa put p0/2 = 675 kPa, beyond p' at peak for all
; three confinements, so every specimen stayed on the dry side
; and the curve SHAPE was always right. Here pc = 460 kPa puts
; the boundary at 230 kPa, barely above sigma3 = 200 kPa
; itself, so the regime flips and the shape is wrong - no peak
; where the laboratory shows a clear peak with softening.
;
; UNIFYING STATEMENT: a single fixed pc misses the confinement
; scaling of strength. When pc is large relative to sigma3 the
; error is quantitative; when pc approaches 2 x sigma3 the
; specimen crosses to the wet side and the error becomes
; qualitative.
;
; ETA PREDICTION UNTESTABLE HERE. The 1.84x / 1.63x strain
; stretches were measured on peak and phase transformation.
; A monotonically hardening curve has neither, so Phase B
; cannot test eta either way.
;
; Servo tracked to 0.06 %; unbalanced force zero throughout.
; The model behaved correctly - the regime placement is a
; consequence of the formulation, not a numerical fault.
;-----------------------------------------------------------
    $ini_pc_lab = 460000.0   ; CALIBRATED (Pa) - sole fitted param
    $ini_pc     = 460000.0   ; UDM fallback, keep equal to above
;
;-----------------------------------------------------------
; NUMERICAL GUARDS - identical to the verified Gai set
;-----------------------------------------------------------
    $p_min    = 1.0          ; floor on mean effective stress
    $pc_min   = 100.0        ; floor on pre-consolidation press.
    $chi_min  = 1.0e-6       ; floor on damage factor
    $r_min    = 1.0e-6       ; floor on sub-loading ratio
    $r_max    = 1.0          ; ceiling on sub-loading ratio
    $kb_dflt  = 1.0e10       ; default bulk modulus bound (Pa)
;
;-----------------------------------------------------------
; SUBZONE ACCUMULATORS - volume weighted, reset each zsub cycle
;-----------------------------------------------------------
    $m_wt_acc   = 0.0        ; accumulated subzone volume
    $m_vol_acc  = 0.0        ; total volumetric strain
    $m_depv_acc = 0.0        ; plastic volumetric strain
    $m_depq_acc = 0.0        ; plastic deviatoric strain
    $m_dept_acc = 0.0        ; plastic strain norm
    $m_p_acc    = 0.0        ; mean effective stress
    $m_q_acc    = 0.0        ; deviatoric stress
    $m_pls_acc  = 0.0        ; plasticity flag
;
end
;
eicp_par_lab
;
;===========================================================
; EOF
;===========================================================
